<title>USA: Chrysler sees higher December sales.</title>
<headline>Chrysler sees higher December sales.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp Vice Chairman Robert Lutz said he expects December car and truck sales figures to be &quot;several percentage points&quot; ahead of last year's level.</p>
<p>In December 1995, Chrysler sold 177,803 cars and trucks in the U.S, a record for the month of December.</p>
<p>Lutz was speaking to reporters at the L.A. Auto Show via satellite from Detroit.</p>
<p>Chrysler is scheduled to report December sales figures on Friday.  </p>
<p>For 1997, Lutz said he expects U.S. car and truck sales to remain fairly stable between 15.1 million and 15.2 million vehicles industrywide, including medium and heavy-duty vehicles.</p>
</text>
